<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="meta">Effective date and last updated: July 22, 2026</p>
<p class="lead">This Privacy Policy explains how the operator of Vokoo (“Vokoo,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, discloses, retains, and protects personal information when you use the Vokoo mobile application, including accounts, profiles, events, messages, videos, voice rooms, virtual items, and related services (collectively, the “Service”). For purposes of applicable privacy law, Vokoo is the controller of personal information described in this Policy unless stated otherwise.</p>
<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p><strong>Account and profile information.</strong> We collect information you provide, including your display name, username, email or other account identifier, profile photo, biography, tags, account preferences, and authentication information. Passwords are protected using one-way security measures and are not displayed back to you.</p>
<p><strong>Content and activity.</strong> We process messages, event participation, follows, reactions, reports, support requests, videos, photos, comments, and other content or actions you choose to provide through the Service.</p>
<p>When you use voice or video features, the Service processes audio or video in real time so participants can communicate. We do not record private voice-room audio unless we clearly notify participants and obtain any consent required by law.</p>
<p><strong>Device, diagnostic, and usage information.</strong> We may receive device model, operating system, app version, language, IP address, approximate region, identifiers used for security, crash diagnostics, feature interactions, and timestamps. We use this information to deliver, secure, support, and improve the Service.</p>
<p><strong>Device permissions.</strong> Camera, microphone, and photo-library access are used only after you grant the relevant permission and only for the feature you request. You may change permissions in device settings. Vokoo does not access your contacts or precise location unless a feature clearly requests that access and you grant permission.</p>
<p><strong>Purchases.</strong> The app store processes payment-card and billing details. We receive transaction status, product, price, currency, and receipt or transaction identifiers needed to deliver purchases, prevent fraud, and provide support, but we do not receive your complete payment-card number.</p>
<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
<ul>
<li>Provide accounts, profiles, events, messaging, video, and voice-room features.</li>
<li>Personalize content and recommend relevant people or activities.</li>
<li>Maintain security, prevent fraud, enforce our rules, and investigate reports.</li>
<li>Respond to support requests and send service-related notices.</li>
<li>Measure performance, diagnose errors, and improve the Service.</li>
<li>Comply with legal obligations and protect users, Vokoo, and the public.</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. Legal Bases and Consent</h2>
<p>Where applicable, we process information to perform our contract with you; pursue legitimate interests such as safety, fraud prevention, support, and service improvement; comply with legal obligations; protect vital interests; and act with your consent. You may withdraw consent through device settings or by contacting us, without affecting processing already performed lawfully.</p>
<h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>
<p>We do not sell personal information and do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We may disclose limited information to hosting, analytics, content-delivery, communications, fraud-prevention, payment-support, moderation, and customer-support providers that process it under contractual restrictions; to other users according to your actions and profile visibility; to professional advisers; in connection with a merger, financing, acquisition, or transfer of assets; or when reasonably necessary to comply with law, enforce our terms, respond to lawful process, or protect safety and rights.</p>
<h2>5. Public Content and Social Features</h2>
<p>Your public profile, posts, event participation, and interactions may be visible to other users. Messages and voice-room participation are visible or audible to their intended participants. Use blocking and reporting controls when needed, and avoid sharing sensitive information publicly.</p>
<h2>6. Retention</h2>
<p>We retain account and profile information while your account is active; transaction records for the period required for accounting, fraud prevention, and legal compliance; reports and safety records as reasonably needed to protect users and enforce our Terms; and diagnostic records for a limited period needed to investigate reliability and security. Retention periods depend on the nature and sensitivity of the information, the purpose for which it was collected, and legal requirements.</p>
<p>After a valid deletion request, we delete or de-identify information within a commercially reasonable period, except where retention is required for security, dispute resolution, legal compliance, prevention of repeat abuse, exercise or defense of legal claims, or fulfillment of transactions. Backup copies expire through normal rotation and are not returned to active use.</p>
<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect information. No electronic service is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. Please protect your credentials and notify us if you suspect unauthorized access.</p>
<h2>8. Your Choices and Rights</h2>
<p>You may update profile information in the app, manage device permissions in system settings, block users, clear local cache, log out, or request account deletion. Depending on your location, you may also request access, correction, portability, restriction, objection, or deletion of personal information and may appeal a denied privacy request.</p>
<p>To exercise a right, email <a href="mailto:support@vokoo.app">support@vokoo.app</a>. We may verify your identity before completing the request. You may also contact your local data-protection authority.</p>
<h2>9. Regional Privacy Rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to know or access personal information; correct inaccurate information; obtain a portable copy; delete information; restrict or object to processing; withdraw consent; opt out of certain disclosures; and appeal a decision. We will not discriminate against you for exercising a privacy right. Authorized agents may submit requests where permitted by law, subject to verification of their authority and your identity.</p>
<h2>10. Children’s Privacy</h2>
<p>The Service is not directed to children under 13, or the higher minimum age required in their jurisdiction. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children below that age. If you believe a child provided information unlawfully, contact us so we can take appropriate action.</p>
<h2>11. International Processing</h2>
<p>Information may be processed in countries other than where you live. Where required, we use recognized safeguards for international transfers and apply the protections described in this Policy.</p>
<h2>12. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>The Service may link to third-party services. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies, and Vokoo is not responsible for services it does not control.</p>
<h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Policy as the Service or law changes. We will post the revised version, update the effective date, and provide additional notice when a change is material. Continued use after the effective date means the revised Policy applies.</p>
<h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
<p>Questions, complaints, and privacy requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:support@vokoo.app">support@vokoo.app</a> with “Privacy Request” in the subject line. Please include your account email, the right you wish to exercise, your jurisdiction, and enough detail for us to understand and respond. We may request additional information solely to verify identity or authority.</p>
